Default to a CDZ BIOS when one is present

The BIOS list is sorted by file name and index 0 is the default, so
MAME's front-sp1.bin wins over its CDZ neocd.bin, and a configured
value that matches no entry also falls back to index 0: every game then
stops at the Front Loader's CD player until START is pressed. A CDZ
boots the game itself and loads at double speed. The family comes from
the file's contents, so any name (neocd_z.rom, neocd.bin, archive#file)
is recognised.

--- a/src/libretro_bios.cpp
+++ b/src/libretro_bios.cpp
@@ -104,6 +104,8 @@
     std::sort(globals.biosList.begin(), globals.biosList.end(), [](const BiosListEntry& a, const BiosListEntry& b) {
         return strcmp(a.description.c_str(), b.description.c_str()) < 0;
     });
+
+    globals.biosIndex = defaultIndex();
 }
 
 // Load, byte swap and patch BIOS
@@ -143,6 +145,24 @@
     return true;
 }
 
+// The list is sorted by file name, so "first" is whichever BIOS sorts
+// lowest - front-sp1.bin among MAME's set - and the Front Loader stops
+// every game at its CD player until START is pressed. A CDZ boots the
+// game itself and loads at double speed, so when one is present it is
+// the default. Names vary too much to hard-code one (neocd_z.rom,
+// neocd.bin, a zip's archive#file): the family comes from the file's
+// contents.
+size_t Libretro::Bios::defaultIndex()
+{
+    for (size_t result = 0; result < globals.biosList.size(); ++result)
+    {
+        if (globals.biosList[result].type.first == ::Bios::Family::CDZ)
+            return result;
+    }
+
+    return 0;
+}
+
